{title: Hope In God}
{subtitle: Psalms 42:11}
{key: Cm}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Cm] | [Bb6] | [Cm] | [Bb] |
| [Ab] | [Cm] [Bb] | [Cm] [Bb] | [Ab] [Bb] |
| [Cm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Deep calls to deep at the [Bb]thunder of waterfalls
[Cm]All your breakers [Bb]and waves have swept over me
[Abmaj7]By day the Lord com[Bb]mands his steadfast [Ab]love
At night his [Bb]song is with me in [Cm]prayer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Why are [Eb]you cast down, my [Bb]soul
O soul, why do [Ab]you groan [Eb]within [Bb]me
Hope [Ab]in God [Eb]for I will [Bb]praise him a[Cm]gain
[Ab]My sal[Bb]vation and my [Cm]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
I say to God my rock [Bb]why have you forgotten me
[Cm]Why must I go about in [Bb]mourning oppressed
The [Ab]enemy presses [Bb]in with cold and si[Ab]lence
My [Bb]bones feel like a deadly [Cm]wound
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Why are [Eb]you cast down, my [Bb]soul
Why do [Ab]you groan [Eb]within [Bb]me
Hope [Ab]in God [Eb]for I will [Bb]praise him a[Cm]gain
[Ab]My sal[Bb]vation and my [Cm]God
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]Adversaries taunt [Bb]me all day [Cm]long
They ask where is your [Ab]God
But the Lord commands [Bb]his love by [Cm]day
His song remains with [Ab]me by [Bb][Cm]night
{end_of_bridge}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Hope [Ab]in God [Eb]for I will [Bb]praise him a[Cm]gain
[Ab]My sal[Bb]vation and my [Cm]God
{end_of_verse}
